  "key_observations_html": "<aside class=\"crypto-story-callout\" aria-labelledby=\"key-obs-callout-title\"><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__title\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" id=\"key-obs-callout-title\">Key observations</p><ul class=\"crypto-story-callout__list\"><li><strong>TMMF distributed value fell 2.7% over 30D:</strong> With distributed value at $12.75B (2.7% lower over 30D), tokenized-cash balances look lighter\u2014suggesting some institutions pulled liquidity or rotated away from TMMF wrappers even if headline product news stayed busy. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tradfi-and-fintech/tempo-earn-embedded-stablecoin-yield-deel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tempo Launches Embedded Yield Product for Platforms, Starting With Deel</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>A global regulatory arbitrage map is emerging:</strong> distributed value clusters into distinct compliance regimes\u2014<strong>U.S. Reg S</strong> ~40% of population AUM (e.g. USYC, USDY); <strong>U.S. Reg D</strong> ~40% of population AUM (e.g. BUIDL, iBENJI); <strong>U.S. mutual fund (N-1A)</strong> ~6% of population AUM (e.g. WTGXX). Issuers appear to anchor products in familiar safe harbors rather than one global standard. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/ecb-digital-euro-privacy-cbdcs-global-scrutiny?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ECB defends digital euro privacy as CBDCs face global scrutiny</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Multi-chain footprints are a distribution signal:</strong> Funds listing many networks with thin holder counts usually signal jurisdictional or distribution reach, not deep secondary liquidity on every chain. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/08/24/standard-chartered-first-bank-to-distribute-anchorpoint-s-hong-kong-dollar-stablecoin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Standard Chartered becomes first bank to distribute Hong Kong dollar stablecoin</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Rates still matter as much as product and chain choice:</strong> Rate and money-market moves can reshape fund-level inflows as quickly as any chain or product launch story. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/08/22/stablecoin-neobank-fasset-lands-usd1-billion-valuation-as-sbi-backs-its-payments-push\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Stablecoin neobank Fasset lands $1 billion valuation as SBI backs its payments push</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Issuer strategies are splitting into two models:</strong> <em>Institutional cash rail</em> programs (low holder counts, large AUM per holder\u2014e.g. USYC, BUIDL, iBENJI, USTB) vs <em>global yield / distribution</em> products (broader holder bases, retail- or UCITS-friendly framing\u2014e.g. USDY, WTGXX, BENJI, USTBL). These behave like different businesses under the same \"tokenized MMF\" label. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/08/24/strategy-raises-usd2-billion-through-mstr-sales-and-creates-new-usd-cash-pool\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Strategy raises $2 billion through MSTR sales and creates new USD Cash pool</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Observations rank fund-level and network aggregates on this page against recent tokenization and money-market headlines. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></aside><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
